From d141a05c14a0840a87ac73e572720befa176c420 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 00:09:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Node machine: C and X write a condition's &&, || and ! as the
 lowering's branches (#2890)

#2889 made the lowering write a statement's condition whose expression, under
its `!`s, is an `&&` or `||` as branches to the statement's own targets, and
a conditional's condition so too; #2893 a value `&&`'s or `||`'s first operand.
The machine had no code for the shape and left those expressions to the
tasks: 9 points of its evaluated nodes on each corpus.

C now gives such an operator a target and a sense in place of a value's
context, the two things a CHECK_LOWER_BRANCH task carries
(node_machine_classify_branches): the record whose label the branch goes to,
or the control's own, and the truth it is taken at. An `&&` where false and
an `||` where true hand both operands theirs; an `&&` where true and an `||`
where false send their first operand the other way to a label of their own
past their second operand; a `!` swaps the sense. A statement's CONDITION
starts with the control's label and the control's sense, which the root's
context carries (a do statement's control branches where its condition
holds). An operand that is no such operator is a value with one more segment
after its row, its test and the branch (node_machine_branch_hook). X writes
no entry for the operator itself but its own label's place; such a record
has one label, so the numbering counts labels where it counted labeled
records. The one sweep (node_machine_lower) writes the same from the tape's
end. At reader time the sense is the parser's: a do statement's condition is
a child of its statement's terminator.

The control's label is outside the expression: on the tape it is
BUSTER_NODE_MACHINE_CONTROL_LABEL, and the shadow takes the stream's branch
for it where its target is the entry of the root's control's target. The
inventory's log keeps each body's first label for that
(CheckLowerOwnerPop.labels).

The shadow's comparison of the one sweep (--fused) now poisons the labels'
entries and the calls' records before the sweep runs. It writes them where
the three sweeps wrote theirs, so an entry it left unwritten read as theirs:
a fault in its second label's entry passed the tests.

Part of #2890.

